-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
(a) busy-alarm-reset - error - bin/fm-watch.sh - ask-user - UNRESOLVED
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Verbatim (truncated by the tool at 1448 chars total):

  The health reset is applied to the busy-no-completed-turn alarm, which the
  intent forbids. Intent PART 4: "Scoped deliberately to the stale alarms only:
  the busy-no-completed-turn alarm asks a different question, and a pane
  producing output while completing no turn is exactly what it exists to catch."
  wedge_timer_check calls health_evidence_reset unconditionally before consulting
  the timer, and the busy call sites (bin/fm-watch.sh:1113 and :1125) pass no
  rendered hash. An absent rendered hash only sets that single component to '?';
  fm_health_sample still reads cpu and children, and fm_health_c… [truncated]

Review summary prose, untruncated:

  `health_evidence_reset` is called unconditionally at the top of
  `wedge_timer_check` (`bin/fm-watch.sh:329`), including from the two
  busy-no-completed-turn call sites (`:1113`, `:1125`). Passing an empty rendered
  hash only makes that *one* component `?` - `cpu` and `children` are still
  sampled and compared, and a busy pane's process-tree CPU advances between polls
  by definition. So the busy alarm resets on essentially every poll and can never
  escalate. The intent explicitly requires the opposite. The comment above the
  call states the scoping; the code does not implement it, and no test covers it.

Why this one matters most, in the captain's framing: this is the mirror-image
failure arriving from the unwatched direction. Not a guard that refuses
everything - an alarm that can never sound.

The test that should have caught it is ALSO defective and must be fixed with the
code. tests/fm-health-evidence.test.sh's ratchet case passes `window_backend()`
returning `none`, so fm_health_sample cannot read cpu or children and the
comparison goes unknown for a reason unrelated to the scoping it claims to prove.
It is vacuous on exactly the property at issue. A fixed version must drive a
backend whose process signals ARE readable and assert that the busy path still
escalates while the stale path still resets.

