What the next round does, in order
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. WAIT for firstmate to confirm the synced base exists. The co-captain syncs
   fork main from upstream by the proven procedure - a true merge commit pushed
   directly, never through a PR. Starting before that defeats the purpose.
2. SUBSUMPTION REVIEW FIRST, before writing any more code. For each of the six
   files above, classify upstream's changes against this branch's:
     subsumed      - upstream already does it; drop ours, carry no duplicate
     conflicting   - same problem solved differently; say which is better and
                     why, in terms of the property protected, never authorship
     complementary - independent, both needed; say how they compose
   Write the classification down as the round's deliverable. It is what stops a
   blind rebase from silently discarding an upstream fix or reintroducing a bug
   upstream already closed.
3. THEN build the Part 4 ratchet-reset against the seam's new shape, plus the
   findings above, with the guard-class mutation requirements unchanged -
   including both mirror-image mutants, time-alone-resets and nothing-resets.

Do not rebase blind and reconcile conflicts as they arise; the classification
comes first. Do not treat upstream as authoritative merely because it is
upstream, nor this branch because it is newer. Do not drop the lab reproduction
fixture beside this file - it is the evidence the cause was proven rather than
inferred, and it survives any rebase.
